### Is there any scientific consensus or genetic evidence indicating that the SARS-CoV-2 virus was artificially engineered or pre-planned rather than originating through natural zoonotic transmission?
Answer: No, there is no genetic evidence or scientific consensus indicating that the SARS-CoV-2 virus was artificially engineered; rather, scientific analysis shows it has a natural origin. According to a study published in *Nature Medicine*, researchers analyzing the virus's public genome sequence data "found no evidence that the virus was made in a laboratory or otherwise engineered." Instead, scientists concluded that the virus is "the product of natural evolution," noting that its distinct molecular backbone and specific mutations in its spike protein "rules out laboratory manipulation as a potential origin for SARS-CoV-2."

Source URL: https://www.scripps.edu/news-and-events/press-room/2020/20200317-andersen-covid-19-coronavirus.html

### Did Bill Gates or the Bill & Melinda Gates Foundation fund or participate in any simulation exercises, such as Event 201 in October 2019, that predicted or planned a coronavirus pandemic prior to the actual outbreak?
Answer: Yes, the Bill & Melinda Gates Foundation partnered with the Johns Hopkins Center for Health Security and the World Economic Forum to host Event 201 in October 2019, which was a tabletop exercise that simulated a global pandemic resulting from a fictional coronavirus. However, this exercise did not predict or plan the actual COVID-19 outbreak; the source notes that "there is no evidence that it was meant to model or engineer the current COVID-19 pandemic," and the Johns Hopkins Center for Health Security explicitly stated that they "did not make a prediction during our tabletop exercise."

Source URL: https://www.usatoday.com/story/news/factcheck/2020/03/26/fact-check-bill-gates-backed-pandemic-exercise-didnt-predict-covid-19/5081854002/

### Does Event 201, a pandemic tabletop exercise hosted in October 2019 by the Johns Hopkins Center for Health Security, the World Economic Forum, and the Bill & Melinda Gates Foundation, constitute proof of pre-planning the COVID-19 pandemic, or was it a standard public health preparedness exercise?
Answer: Event 201 does not constitute proof of pre-planning the COVID-19 pandemic; rather, it was a standard public health preparedness exercise. According to the search result, "the fact it took place just before the pandemic started doesn’t mean the organisers had any secret knowledge." The organizers modeled a fictional coronavirus based on scientific expertise and previous outbreaks like SARS and MERS, explicitly stating that the exercise "was not a prediction." Instead, the simulation was run because "the world has seen a 'growing number of epidemic events'" and experts agreed that a global pandemic was inevitable, making preparedness exercises a standard response to what the scientific community already knew about pandemics.

Source URL: https://fullfact.org/health/event-201-coronavirus-pandemic/

