### Did the Bill & Melinda Gates Foundation or any associated entities hold patents on the SARS-CoV-2 virus or COVID-19 vaccines prior to the outbreak of the pandemic in late 2019?
Answer: No, neither the Bill & Melinda Gates Foundation nor associated entities like the Pirbright Institute held patents on the SARS-CoV-2 virus or COVID-19 vaccines prior to the outbreak. While the Pirbright Institute (which has received grants from the Gates Foundation) was granted a patent in 2018, it covers an "attenuated (weakened) form of the coronavirus that could potentially be used as a vaccine to prevent respiratory diseases in birds" and other animals, not SARS-CoV-2. The institute clarified that "Pirbright does not hold any patents on parts of or the complete genome of the SARS-CoV-2 betacoronavirus," and the Gates Foundation is not involved in patenting any potential COVID-19 vaccine.

